.TH WERKMEISTER-NOTES 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-notes \- Workspace notes (.werkmeister/notes/). \fBcontext\fR prints the latest handoff + open decisions for session\-start injection (hook target); \fBgraduate\fR scaffolds an open decision note into the standards tree.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister notes\fR <action> [note_num]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-domain <domain>\fR
graduate: target \e<domain> in the standards tree (omit to infer from refs, or prompt)
.TP
\fB\-\-kind <kind>\fR
graduate: content kind to scaffold (omit to prompt)
.TP
\fB\-\-slug <slug>\fR
graduate: override the derived reference\-file slug
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBcontext\fR prints the workspace's notes context for a fresh Claude Code window. It is the SessionStart hook's target: it reads the hook's payload on stdin, never fails, and always exits 0.
.PP
\fBgraduate\fR scaffolds an open \fBdecision\fR note into the standards tree. At a terminal it asks for the domain and kind; otherwise pass \fB\-\-domain\fR and \fB\-\-kind\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister notes context
werkmeister notes graduate 3 \-\-domain testing \-\-kind rule
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
